Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 03:26:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional lottery engine bridge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Setting lottery_upstream_url in the admin panel makes every lottery endpoint
(rounds, results, odds, bets, records, win/loss, balance and the game-wallet
transfer) come from that engine instead of the local generator in
_bootstrap.php. Clearing the setting reverts instantly.

- api/_lottery_upstream.php: the bridge — forwards the player's own token,
  keeps the site's JSON dialect, and moves money with an idempotent orderId
  (debit here first, credit upstream, refund on failure)
- api/_bootstrap.php: loads the bridge when the file is present
- api/_router.php: tries the engine before the local handler
- api/_draw_router.php: issue and history come from the engine
- if the engine is unreachable every hook returns null and the existing local
  code answers, so the site cannot go dark

Nothing else changes: same URLs, same responses, same login.
